abstract: 'MATLAB software for analysing stratified-plume experiments from Arij Asad''s PhD research,
  Mixing behaviour of plumes, at the University of Bristol. It provides greyscale stratification-depth
  measurements, density reconstruction from fluorescence images, image-edge separation measurements and
  refractive-index matching calculations.


  The software follows the thesis greyscale method: first-frame background subtraction, normalisation
  within each frame, and the first upward crossing of a fixed dimensionless threshold. Central thresholds
  and sensitivity ranges reproduce Table 2.4. Supporting documentation is provided in the folder READMEs.


  Density reconstruction adapts Horne-Jones et al. (2026), Section 3.2, equations (16)-(18), doi:10.1007/s00348-026-04249-4.
  This attribution applies to the density-reconstruction method. MATLAB and Image Processing Toolbox are
  required. Experimental images, measured calibration inputs and completed run settings are supplied by
  the user.


  Source code is licensed under MIT; thesis figures and documentation are licensed under CC BY 4.0.'
